    <string name="connection_screen_info"><![CDATA[

    To proceed to the next screen, press and hold the <b>LOWER-LEFT</b> button on the watch for 3 seconds.
    After the second double-beep, the app will display the time-setting screen.
    <p><b>Make sure the official Casio app is not running, as it will interfere with this app.</b></p>
    <p>Some watches, like the DW-H5600, require pairing before they can connect for the first time.
    In such cases, put your watch into pairing mode. A pop-up will appear on your phone prompting you to pair with the watch.</p>
    <p>To run Actions defined in the <b>Actions</b> screen, short-press the <b>LOWER-RIGHT</b> button. Actions are apps on your phone, like <b>Take a photo</b>.
    Using actions, the watch acts like a remote control for your phone.</p>
    <p>You can download this app from <a href="https://f-droid.org/en/packages/com.beamburst.casswatch">F-DROID</a></p>

    ]]></string>

    <string name="alarms_screen_info"><![CDATA[The <b>B5600/B5000/B2100/ABL-100</b> watches have 5 alarms shown here.
    The alarms can be updated by pressing on the time value of each alarm. A new dialog will appear, which allows you to set the alarm\'s time.
    Once the alarms have been set, you can send them to the watch, or send them to the Alarm Clock app on the phone.]]></string>
    <string name="events_screen_info"><![CDATA[This screen displays Events from your <b>Google Calendar</b> and allows you to send them to the watch\'s
    <b>reminders</b>.\n\nIf no events appear, make sure you have future events, or non-expired repeating events in your Google calendar.]]>
</string>
